# dispatch-env.tmpl — environment file template for the dispatch service.
# Two-user: copy to /home/dispatch-svc/.env. Single-user: copy to ~/.config/agent-gtd-dispatch/env. Fill in real values.
# All lines beginning with # are comments.

# =============================================================================
# Required variables
# =============================================================================

# Dispatch API auth — callers must provide this as a Bearer token.
# Auto-minted by setup-dispatch-host.sh Step 3.5 if left empty. Leave blank for fresh installs;
# do NOT clear an existing value on a true-up run (would silently break app-side pairing —
# re-register the new value in the GTD UI manually if rotating).
DISPATCH_API_KEY=

# Agent GTD API (for fetching items/projects and posting comments).
# The agent's agent-gtd MCP server is <AGENT_GTD_URL>/mcp, registered as an HTTP /mcp
# server by scripts/kb-mcp-refresh.sh (setup Step 4.6 and every deploy.sh). The URL
# must serve <AGENT_GTD_URL>/mcp over a TLS certificate Node trusts by default, since
# Claude Code (Node) connects to it directly. AGENT_GTD_API_KEY is never written into
# that registration; agents send their per-run callback token instead.
AGENT_GTD_URL=https://gtd.example.com
AGENT_GTD_API_KEY=agtd_...

# Anthropic API key — used ONLY by the in-process rollout planner (POST /plan).
# NOT forwarded to the dispatched Claude Code subprocess: engines.py allowlists only
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN for the claude engine, so this key never reaches the agent
# process. Forwarding it would flip billing off the Max/OAuth subscription onto
# pay-per-token API (see kb-01512).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# =============================================================================
# Two-user split: agent subprocess user
# =============================================================================

# Username of the unprivileged agent user that owns workspace directories.
# Must match the --agent-user argument used when running setup-dispatch-host.sh.
# When set, the service spawns agent subprocesses via `sudo -u <value> -H`.
# Leave empty to disable user-switching (dev/test only).
#
# In single-user mode (DISPATCH_SINGLE_USER=1 at setup time), this MUST be left
# empty — the runtime _sudo_wrap shortcut is what gates single-user behaviour.
# setup-dispatch-host.sh strips this line from the .env if it appears under
# single-user mode.
DISPATCH_AGENT_SUBPROCESS_USER=dispatch

# =============================================================================
# Optional variables
# =============================================================================

# Maximum concurrent agent runs — set per host based on core count.
# Formula: num_cores × 1.5; e.g. 4 cores → 6, 8 cores → 12.
# Default (32) is too high for Pi-class hosts (e.g. a 4-core Pi 5).
# See kb-01544 for capacity sizing rationale.
# DISPATCH_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=6

# Workspace root for cloned repos (default: ~/workspace, relative to
# DISPATCH_AGENT_SUBPROCESS_USER's home when user-switching is enabled).
# DISPATCH_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/home/dispatch/workspace

# Claude Code turn and timeout limits.
# DISPATCH_MAX_TURNS=50
# DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# Ollama local inference — set OLLAMA_BASE_URL to route claude-code-ollama
# dispatches through a local Ollama instance instead of the Anthropic API.
# Root URL, no /v1 suffix (e.g. http://<ollama-host>:11434).
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=ollama
# OLLAMA_DEFAULT_MODEL=qwen3.6:35b

# Ollama CLOUD (https://ollama.com) — a single key powers THREE cloud engines:
#   talos-glm        (talos loop → glm-5.3:cloud, Ollama native /api/chat)
#   talos-glm-flash  (talos loop → glm-5.3-flash:cloud, Ollama native /api/chat)
#   claude-code-glm  (Claude Code loop → glm-5.3:cloud, /v1/messages)
# Get a non-expiring key at https://ollama.com/settings/keys. Distinct from the
# LOCAL OLLAMA_API_KEY above — never a fallback between them. Overriding the base
# URL / model is rarely needed (defaults: https://ollama.com, glm-5.3:cloud).
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com
# OLLAMA_CLOUD_MODEL=glm-5.3:cloud

# Talos engine binary path — managed by setup-dispatch-host.sh --with-talos.
# Set automatically when --with-talos is passed to the installer; override here
# only if you place the binary at a non-standard path.
# TALOS_BIN=
# TALOS_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECS=900  # raises talos' 300 s gate-command default for cold Pi runs

# =============================================================================
# Bedrock provider (corporate/port environments only)
# =============================================================================
# Use these when the Anthropic API is unreachable (e.g. corporate egress policy
# routes Claude access through Amazon Bedrock instead). The planner only uses
# these settings; build/manage agent subprocesses are unaffected.
#
# Provider gate: set to 'bedrock' to enable. Default 'anthropic' keeps the
# existing Anthropic API path byte-for-byte unchanged.
# DISPATCH_PLANNER_PROVIDER=anthropic
#
# Bedrock model ID. The global cross-region inference endpoint is the default;
# use the us. regional CRIS variant (e.g. us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6) if
# your environment requires data-residency guarantees (+10% pricing applies).
# DISPATCH_PLANNER_BEDROCK_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
#
# AWS region for Bedrock API calls. IMPORTANT: the anthropic SDK reads
# AWS_REGION; if unset it defaults to us-east-1. AWS_PROFILE alone does NOT
# supply the region — the SDK does not read ~/.aws/config for the region.
# Credentials are resolved from the default AWS credential chain (AWS_PROFILE,
# env vars, instance metadata, etc.).
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# =============================================================================
# Authentication extras (must survive sudo boundary — listed in sudoers env_keep)
# =============================================================================

# Claude Code OAuth token — alternative to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for OAuth-based
# authentication to Anthropic. Set this instead of ANTHROPIC_API_KEY when using
# Claude Code's OAuth login flow.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# KB_DATABASE_URL — RETIRED and FORBIDDEN. Agents reach the KB only through the
# hosted KB MCP servers (PERSONAL_KB_URL / PERSONAL_KB_API_KEY below). A
# live-KB DSN here once reached agent subprocesses, where a repo's test suite opened
# production Postgres. setup-dispatch-host.sh strips it (and TEAM_KB_DATABASE_URL /
# KB_SERVICE_DATABASE_URL) from the service env on every run. Do not set it.

# Local test-Postgres DSN for @pytest.mark.postgres suites (e.g. kb-core) run by
# dispatched agents, and the flag that turns a missing DSN into a hard test
# failure rather than a silent skip. Both are written automatically by
# setup-dispatch-host.sh (Postgres is default-on; --without-postgres removes them) — do not set these by hand.
# KB_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
# KB_REQUIRE_POSTGRES_TESTS=

# TEAM_KB_DATABASE_URL — RETIRED and FORBIDDEN (stripped by setup-dispatch-host.sh).
# The team-kb MCP server is a hosted HTTP server; see TEAM_KB_URL / TEAM_KB_API_KEY below.

# Anthropic API key for the KB MCP servers' own LLM calls — RETIRED — no longer read
# by installer Step 4.6. Both KB MCP servers are now thin HTTP clients of a hosted KB
# web service and make no LLM calls of their own.
# KB_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Hosted personal KB service URL + API key. Read by installer Step 4.6 and deploy.sh
# (not the service) via scripts/kb-mcp-refresh.sh. PERSONAL_KB_URL is the service base
# URL; `/mcp` is appended to register personal-kb as an HTTP MCP server. The key is
# written to `~/.personal_kb_hook_key` (0600) in the agent home and never into
# `~/.claude.json`. personal-kb is skipped when either is unset. No sudoers env_keep
# entry is needed: the values are applied at provision/deploy time, not inherited by
# the agent subprocess at run time.
# PERSONAL_KB_URL=
# PERSONAL_KB_API_KEY=
# KB API key handed to talos runs as PERSONAL_KB_API_KEY (paired with PERSONAL_KB_URL
# above). Use a key minted for talos. Talos runs get no KB access when it is unset.
# TALOS_PERSONAL_KB_API_KEY=
# TALOS_MEMORY=off
# One of off | annotate | deny-once; passed to every talos fleet run as --memory.
# An unknown value is treated as off. Needs TALOS_PERSONAL_KB_API_KEY to reach a remote KB.

# Hosted team KB service URL + API key. Read by installer Step 4.6 and deploy.sh via
# scripts/kb-mcp-refresh.sh. TEAM_KB_URL is the service base URL; `/mcp` is appended
# to register team-kb as an HTTP MCP server. The key is written to `~/.team_kb_key`
# (0600) in the agent home and never into `~/.claude.json`. team-kb is skipped when
# either is unset. No sudoers env_keep entry is needed, for the same reason as
# PERSONAL_KB_URL above.
# TEAM_KB_URL=
# TEAM_KB_API_KEY=

# Agent identity name — used for GTD comment attribution so comments appear
# under a specific agent name (e.g. claude-build-abc12345) rather than the
# generic service identity.
# AGENT_GTD_AGENT_NAME=
